  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Skies are mostly cloudy this afternoon\nacross northern and central Nevada. There are weak returns noted\non radar and remote observation platforms are picking very light\nprecipitation at this time, mainly over north-central Humboldt and\nnorth-central Elko counties. For tonight through tomorrow morning,\na weak shortwave will move across the forecast area. Very little\nin the way of precipitation is expected. Overnight lows tonight\nwill be in the 20s. Highs Monday will be in the upper 30s to 40s.\nWinds are expected to remain light. There is a twenty to thirty\npercent probability for patchy freezing fog during the overnight\nMonday into Tuesday as any remaining snow melts in the valley\nlocations and these have been highlighted in the weather grids.\nOvernight lows will be in the teens and 20s.\n\nOn Tuesday, all models continue to depict an upper level ridge\nbuilding across northern and central Nevada. Conditions are\nexpected to be mostly sunny with highs warming into the 40s. Winds\nwill be light through the afternoon with occasional gusts to 15\nmph. Look for the dry and quiet weather to continue Tuesday night\nand Wednesday as the ridge axis maximizes over the area, then\nmoves off to the east. Lows will be in the 20s for the most part.\n\nAn upper level trough is forecast to wobble in the Gulf of Alaska,\nwith upper level energy peeling off the main trough and moving\ninto California, then across northern Nevada early Wednesday\nthrough early Thursday. Not much moisture and instability is \ncurrently associated with this feature as models have trended\nweaker over the past several runs. Highs Wednesday and Thursday\nare now in the 40s to near 50 on Wednesday to upper 40s and low\n50s for Thursday. Overnight lows will be in the teens and 20s for\nWednesday and Thursday mornings, warming into the 20s to 30s for\nFriday morning. Winds are expected to be light, though some gusts\nto 25 mph are possible along the northern border with Idaho for \nThursday afternoon. \n\nGeneral ridging is expected through the weekend with the\npossibility of a trough by Saturday night and Sunday. Highs will\nbe in the 40s and 50s with lows in the 20s.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Confidence remains moderate \nwith the low probability of precipitation during the overnight \nover the north but confidence has diminished in precipitation \nchances as model runs continue to erode moisture availability with\nincoming systems. Confidence is now moderate with respect to the\nupper ridge building in during the week with afternoon highs\ntrending above normal.",
